.TH MW-MCP 1 "2026-09-06" "MemoryWhale 0.10.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
mw-mcp \- Model Context Protocol server over MemoryWhale memory
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mw-mcp
.RB [ --list-tools ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B mw-mcp
is a Model Context Protocol (MCP) server that lets an AI agent query your
MemoryWhale memory directly, instead of pasting it in. It speaks
newline-delimited JSON-RPC 2.0 on standard input and output. Use
.B --list-tools
to print the runtime tool names and exit. It reads the same local database as
the rest of the CLI and honours
.BR MEMORYWHALE_DATA_DIR .
.PP
Register it once with an MCP client, e.g. Claude Code:
.PP
.RS
.B claude mcp add memorywhale -- mw-mcp
.RE
.PP
For Claude Code or Rho capture hooks and memory-use guidance as well as MCP
registration, use
.B mw integrate claude
or
.BR "mw integrate rho" .
MCP alone does not automatically capture terminal or agent commands.
.SH PROTOCOL AND TRUST
Supports revision 2026-07-28 with per-request metadata and server/discover,
plus legacy 2025-11-25 and 2024-11-05 initialization. Stdio has no network
listener or separate protocol authentication: trust is inherited from the
spawning client and OS user. Trusted clients can read evidence and explicitly
save lessons. The same tools are available at POST /mcp through
.BR mw-serve (1),
with Bearer authentication when that listener uses a token.
.SH TOOLS
.TP
.B recent_errors
Recent failed commands (non-zero exit) with their error output.
.TP
.B search_memory
Search remembered commands, arguments, output, and notes for a term.
Requires query; optional project, machine, and agent filters scope retrieval.
.TP
.B get_context
Ranked memory context, optionally scoped by project, machine, and agent.
The agent filter accepts claude, rho, or terminal; terminal matches NULL
provenance including manual and legacy records. Agent is separate from source.
.TP
.B remember
Save a freeform lesson or conclusion for later, so a future
.B search_memory
or
.B get_context
call finds it instead of re-deriving it.
Requires text. Agent-authored lessons are pending review by default and do not
enter retrieval until approved. This is the only tool that writes memory.
.TP
.B similar_failures
Find evidence of prior occurrences and later successful runs. Requires
error_text; optional command enables exact fingerprint matching.
.TP
.B stats
Read the memory count, failure count, most recent timestamp, and database path.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B MEMORYWHALE_DATA_DIR
Override the data directory (default
.IR <data_local>/MemoryWhale ).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR mw (1),
.BR mw-serve (1)
